---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";

const basePath = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<DocsLayout
  title="MCP servers"
  description="Add and manage user-scoped MCP servers in Veasel Code, trust them per session, and approve every tool call."
>
  <section class="doc-page">
    <p class="kicker">FIELD GUIDE / MCP</p>
    <h1>
      Connect tools.
      <br />
      <em>Keep every call in view.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Veasel can use Model Context Protocol servers from operator-managed user
      config or from experimental Agent Plugin packages. Trust is per session;
      every model-requested tool call still pauses for inspection and one-time
      approval.
    </p>

    <div class="compatibility-banner">
      <span class="compatibility-mark" aria-hidden="true">
        ⌘
      </span>
      <div>
        <strong>User-scoped add/manage ships today</strong>
        <p>
          Add stdio or Streamable HTTP servers with <code>/mcp add</code> or{" "}
          <code>POST /v1/mcp-servers</code>. Config persists in{" "}
          <code>$VEASEL_DATA_DIR/mcp-servers.json</code> (owner-only mode when
          the OS supports it). Capability: <code>mcp.servers.configured</code>.
          Project-scoped MCP files and OAuth remain open.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Add a user-scoped server (TUI)</h2>
      <p>
        In a session, type <code>/</code> for slash suggestions, then manage
        configured servers:
      </p>
      <pre><code>/mcp add stdio memory npx -y @modelcontextprotocol/server-memory
/mcp add http docs https://mcp.example.com/mcp
/mcp
/mcp enable memory
/mcp disable memory
/mcp remove memory</code></pre>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li>
          <code>stdio</code> — bare <code>PATH</code> command or absolute
          regular file; optional absolute <code>cwd</code> via the API. Veasel
          does not download packages or run install scripts for you.
        </li>
        <li>
          <code>http</code> — Streamable HTTP URL with the same origin and
          header rules as plugin MCP (HTTPS or loopback; redirects refused).
        </li>
        <li>
          Names identify the server under the synthetic catalog package{" "}
          <code>configured</code>. List views omit header/env secret values.
        </li>
        <li>
          Disabled servers leave durable config in place but drop out of the
          plugin catalog until re-enabled.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Trust, then approve each call</h2>
      <p>
        Adding a server does not grant the model access. Trust it for the
        current session, then review every tool call:
      </p>
      <pre><code>/mcp trust configured/memory
/mcp untrust configured/memory

/mcp calls
/mcp call show &lt;id&gt;
/mcp call approve &lt;id&gt;   # or reject</code></pre>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li>
          Plugin-packaged servers still use{" "}
          <code>/mcp trust &lt;plugin&gt;/&lt;server&gt;</code>.
        </li>
        <li>
          The review screen states that the call has not reached its server yet.
          Rejected or interrupted calls are not replayed.
        </li>
        <li>
          Trusted stdio processes inherit the server user and are{" "}
          <strong>not</strong> OS-sandboxed. Inspect effects before approval.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>HTTP API</h2>
      <p>
        Operator config (user scope) is separate from per-session trust and
        per-call approval:
      </p>
      <div
        class="provider-table api-table"
        role="table"
        aria-label="Configured MCP API endpoints"
      >
        <div class="provider-table-row provider-table-head" role="row">
          <b role="columnheader">Method</b>
          <b role="columnheader">Path</b>
          <b role="columnheader">Purpose</b>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">GET · POST</b>
          <code role="cell">/v1/mcp-servers</code>
          <span role="cell">
            List or upsert user-scoped configured servers (secrets omitted from
            views).
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">PATCH · DELETE</b>
          <code role="cell">{"/v1/mcp-servers/{name}"}</code>
          <span role="cell">Enable/disable or remove a configured server.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">GET · POST</b>
          <code role="cell">{"/v1/sessions/{id}/mcp-servers"}</code>
          <span role="cell">
            List or update per-session trust (
            <code>plugin_name=configured</code> for user-added servers).
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">GET · POST</b>
          <code role="cell">{"/v1/sessions/{id}/mcp-tool-calls…"}</code>
          <span role="cell">
            Inspect, approve, or reject one pending tool call.
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <pre><code>curl -sS http://127.0.0.1:4097/v1/mcp-servers
curl -sS -X POST http://127.0.0.1:4097/v1/mcp-servers \
  -H 'content-type: application/json' \
  -d '&#123;&quot;name&quot;:&quot;memory&quot;,&quot;transport&quot;:&quot;stdio&quot;,&quot;command&quot;:&quot;npx&quot;,&quot;args&quot;:[&quot;-y&quot;,&quot;@modelcontextprotocol/server-memory&quot;]&#125;'
curl -sS -X PATCH http://127.0.0.1:4097/v1/mcp-servers/memory \
  -H 'content-type: application/json' \
  -d '&#123;&quot;enabled&quot;:false&#125;'</code></pre>
      <p>
        Full request and response shapes live in the runtime{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/veasel-labs/veasel/blob/main/docs/openapi.yaml">
          OpenAPI contract
        </a>
        .
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Plugin-packaged MCP</h2>
      <p>
        Agent Plugin packages under <code>$VEASEL_PLUGIN_DIR</code> or{" "}
        <code>$VEASEL_DATA_DIR/plugins</code> may declare stdio or Streamable
        HTTP servers in <code>mcp.json</code>. Those appear in the plugin
        catalog (<code>GET /v1/plugins</code>), not under{" "}
        <code>/v1/mcp-servers</code>. Local directory links can be managed with{" "}
        <code>/plugin add|remove</code> and <code>/v1/plugins/links</code> —
        Veasel does not fetch remote packages. See the{" "}
        <a href={`${basePath}/docs/plugins/`}>plugins ledger</a> for conformance
        status.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Still open</h2>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li>Project-scoped MCP config files (writable workspace files).</li>
        <li>OAuth for remote MCP servers.</li>
        <li>
          Full Agent Plugins v1.0.0 conformance and OS sandboxing for stdio MCP.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <aside class="callout">
      <strong>Untrusted by default.</strong> MCP tool output is reference
      context for the model. Skill scripts and MCP install scripts are never
      auto-executed. Prefer reviewing arguments when a call could change files,
      talk to the network, or touch secrets.
    </aside>

    <p class="doc-next">
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/docs/security/`}>
        Security boundary <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/docs/api/`}>
        API & headless <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/docs/plugins/`}>
        Plugins ledger <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
